============================================================
Keavi LLC — Concord (proprietary, first-party)
============================================================

Release builds of this product include Concord, a proprietary on-device
correction engine developed by Keavi LLC
(https://github.com/keavi-app/concord). Concord is provided under a
proprietary license, distributed only inside Parleq.app, and is not
available separately or as source. The public open-source build of Parleq
does not include it (it is gated behind the `Concord` SwiftPM trait).

Concord bundles two permissively-licensed third-party data sets, which
therefore ship inside Parleq.app (Concord builds only):

  * CMUdict — 2-clause BSD — a derived, compressed form of the CMU
    Pronouncing Dictionary (cmusphinx/cmudict, pinned commit
    74790861f652b15e4ac49015a90074ad62a27690), Copyright (c) 1993–2015
    Carnegie Mellon University. https://github.com/cmusphinx/cmudict
  * panphon — MIT — articulatory feature-table values extracted into
    Concord's generated ArpabetToIPA.swift and PanphonFeatureTable.swift,
    Copyright (c) 2015 Carnegie Mellon University (David R. Mortensen).
    https://github.com/dmort27/panphon

