============================================================
FluidAudio
============================================================

This product uses FluidAudio (Apache-2.0) for local speech recognition
on Apple Neural Engine. It is pinned to a fork (jonyoder/FluidAudio, tag
0.15.4-encoder.1) of the upstream FluidInference/FluidAudio 0.15.4 line,
carrying an opt-in, additive patch that exposes the Parakeet encoder
feature sequence used by the on-device voice-enrollment (voiceprint)
disambiguation gate. The fork remains Apache-2.0.

  * FluidAudio (fork)  https://github.com/jonyoder/FluidAudio
  * FluidAudio (upstream)  https://github.com/FluidInference/FluidAudio

FluidAudio downloads CoreML model weights at runtime from
Hugging Face (FluidInference's published Parakeet TDT v3 and CTC
checkpoints). The model weights are not redistributed inside the
.app bundle and are governed by the upstream NVIDIA NeMo model
license terms posted at the corresponding Hugging Face repositories.
See THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md § "Model weights" for details.

FluidAudio embeds two components in its speaker-diarization
clustering that compile into this .app and require attribution on
binary redistribution:

  * fastcluster — 2-clause BSD — Copyright (c) 2011 Daniel Müllner;
    changes from version 1.1.24 on (c) Google Inc.
  * VBx — Apache-2.0 — Brno University of Technology (BUT Speech@FIT).

Their full license texts ship in FluidAudio's source checkout under
ThirdPartyLicenses/. See THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md § "Embedded
components" for details.

